;
; DEVS:Internet/routes
;
; The default route: the address of the router that receives everything that
; is not on the local network.
;
; This is the file that Roadshow uses.  Roadshow 1.15 has no
; DEVS:Internet/default_gateway, although some secondary sources say
; otherwise -- AmiNetXDuo reads one if it finds it, because its own design
; notes asked for it and a file that exists must not be ignored.
;
; With DHCP this file is not necessary.  The address of the router arrives
; with the lease.
;

; DEFAULT -- the router.  Usually the address that ends in .1 or .254 on the
; local network.  DEFAULTGATEWAY= is accepted as a synonym.
;
DEFAULT=192.168.1.1

; A route to one particular network, through some other gateway.  DST names
; the destination, VIA the gateway to reach it through.  NETDST and HOSTDST
; say explicitly whether the destination is a network or a single machine.
;
; AmiNetXDuo parses these and does not install them yet -- only the default
; route is acted on.
;
;DST=10.0.0.0    VIA=192.168.1.254
;HOSTDST=10.1.2.3 VIA=192.168.1.254
